&lt;p>The cytoplasm those chains fold in is crowded. Diffusion there is not the diffusion of one protein in a large box of water. A periodic cell with one protein and a bath answers a different physical question.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>About 20,000 protein-coding genes is the right order for the human set. It is not 20,000 structures. Alternative splicing and post-translational modification produce many chains from one gene. An AlphaFold model, or a PDB entry, is one sequence in one conformation. The
is about whether that conformation is even a plausible fold, which comes before the question of whether it is the conformation that binds.&lt;/p>
&lt;h2 id="charge-is-four-terms-in-a-force-field">Charge is four terms in a force field&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>Amino acids differ in charge and polarity. The chain is synthesized as a line, and that line collapses into a fold. A force field does not carry this as one interaction called charge.&lt;/p>
&lt;figure style="margin:2rem 0;">
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 720 360" role="img" aria-labelledby="prot-ff-title prot-ff-desc" style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block;">
