&lt;p>Partial charges are a model of the electrostatic box, assigned before the dynamics, and they depend on the protonation you chose. Histidine, aspartate, glutamate, and the termini are the usual decisions. The
is about how much that assignment moves a docking score. It does not make the score a free energy. A quantum calculation on the ligand, as in the
, reports the electrons of that molecule. It does not fold the protein and it does not prove the complex.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>The hydrophobic effect is why an implicit-solvent or vacuum model can fold the wrong core. The chain is not clicking together by electrostatics alone. If the simulation has no water, or a solvent model that ignores that term, the compact structure it finds is answering a different physical question.&lt;/p>
&lt;h2 id="allostery-is-a-shift-in-how-often-each-shape-appears">Allostery is a shift in how often each shape appears&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>A folded chain presents a surface. A partner binds, the local charge distribution changes, and the shape changes with it. A site that was hidden can open, the protein can join a larger assembly, or the new surface can pass a signal on. The error is to treat the protein as one shape that snaps to a second shape.&lt;/p>
&lt;figure style="margin:2rem 0;">
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 720 260" role="img" aria-labelledby="prot-allo-title prot-allo-desc" style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block;">
&lt;title id="prot-allo-title">Binding shifts which conformer is common&lt;/title>
&lt;desc id="prot-allo-desc">Without ligand, a closed shape is common and an open shape is rare, and the site is buried. With ligand, the open shape is common and the ligand sits between the two lobes.&lt;/desc>
&lt;g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity="0.3" stroke-width="1.5">
&lt;rect x="16" y="16" width="330" height="228" rx="14"/>
&lt;rect x="360" y="16" width="344" height="228" rx="14"/>
&lt;/g>
&lt;g fill="currentColor" font-family="system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',sans-serif" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" font-weight="700">
&lt;text x="120" y="44">No ligand&lt;/text>
