&lt;p>Protein-coding exons are on the order of one percent of the human genome. The rest includes introns, regulatory sequence, and a great deal of repetitive DNA. A simulation never sees that rest. It sees the chain you chose, in the protonation you chose, in the box you built.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>The calculation ends at whichever object in Figure 1 the question actually named.&lt;/p>
